title Agent multi-step tool loop — PLAN, concurrent EXECUTE, SYNTHESIZE; step guard and step failure\n(evidence: orchestrator/app/engines/agent.py:36-658 · orchestrator/app/main.py:592-601 · orchestrator/app/llm.py:78,215-262 · orchestrator/app/engines/sql.py:179-212 · orchestrator/app/engines/live_sf.py:140-148 · orchestrator/app/engines/search.py:416,446,454)

participant "frontend\nsse.ts · mergeStep · step list UI" as fe #2563EB
participant "orchestrator · worker()\nmain.py:592-601" as orch #7C3AED
participant "engines/agent · LangGraph subgraph\nplan → execute → synthesize (agent.py:609-628)" as ag #7C3AED
participant "execute_steps()\nSemaphore(3) · agent.py:369-405" as exec #7C3AED
participant "sub-engines (lazily imported)\nsql · rag · live_sf · search" as sub #7C3AED
participant "vllm (MAIN)\nOPENAI_BASE_URL" as vmain #16A34A
participant "DuckDB warehouse\nLanceDB" as store #D97706

box "Egress outside the host" #FEF2F2
participant "Salesforce org" as sf #64748B
participant "searxng + arbitrary\npublic websites" as web #64748B
end box

autonumber

orch -> ag : run_agent_engine(message, history, emit,\neffort, salesforce = (mode != "assistant"), web = want_search)\nin-process await · main.py:592-601, agent.py:631-658

== 1 · PLAN — one shot, one retry, then a degraded fallback ==

loop for _attempt in range(2) — agent.py:197
  ag -> vmain : HTTP POST /v1/chat/completions · JSON · async\ntemperature 0.1 · max_tokens 6000 · system = _PLAN_SYSTEM or _PLAN_SYSTEM_NO_SF\nagent.py:188-210
  vmain --> ag : raw plan text
  ag -> ag : parse_agent_plan → pydantic AgentPlan\nsteps 1..MAX_STEPS=8, unique ids, kind in (sql, rag, llm, web, salesforce)\nagent.py:59-97
  alt parse or transport failed
    ag -> ag : last_error = str(exc)[:400], appended to the retry prompt as an extra user turn\nagent.py:200-214
  end
end

alt both attempts failed
  ag -> ag : _fallback_plan(message) — a SINGLE kind="llm" step titled message[:60]\nagent.py:145-148, :215
  note over ag #FEE2E2
    The retry loop catches **every** Exception including timeouts and 400s
    (agent.py:213-214) and logs nothing. A deep multi-tool request silently
    collapses into one plain completion, and the user is never told: the
    degraded plan streams a normal answer with route "agent".
  end note
end

ag -> ag : coerce_allowed(plan, web=state["web"]) — mutates PlanStep.kind **in place**\nagent.py:164-174, :561-568

note over ag #FFFBEB
  **MAX-ITERATION GUARD — there is no iteration.** The subgraph is
  plan → execute → synthesize → END with **no cycle** (agent.py:614-617) and
  no step can enqueue another, so the loop cannot run away. The bound is
  purely on step *count*, enforced twice:
  · pydantic max_length = MAX_STEPS = 8 (agent.py:36, :67)
  · the prompt budget step_budget(effort): medium 5, high 8 (agent.py:42, :48)
  applied by **string substitution** on the literal "at most 8 " (agent.py:190) —
  if either prompt constant is reworded, the budget silently stops applying.
  _STEP_BUDGET and _SYNTH_TOKENS have no "fast"/"low" keys, so an explicit
  agent=true at effort "fast" silently gets the medium values.
end note

== 2 · EXECUTE — asyncio.gather over the plan, at most 3 at a time ==

ag -> exec : execute_steps(plan, history, emit, salesforce, effort, message)\nagent.py:571-580
note over ag, exec #FEE2E2
  **F7 — the `web` gate is enforced only at plan time.** _execute_node does
  not forward `web` (agent.py:571-580), so a step that survived coercion
  still reaches the live web branch at agent.py:337.
end note

loop for each PlanStep, up to STEP_CONCURRENCY = 3 concurrently (agent.py:378-381)
  exec -> fe : SSE · event: step\ndata: {"id": int, "title": str, "status": "running"}\nagent.py:381-382

  alt kind == "sql" and salesforce
    exec -> sub : generate_and_run_sql(step.input, history=list(history))\nagent.py:257
    sub -> vmain : SQL generation, then the chart-spec call · 1-2 completions\nsql.py:210-212
    sub -> store : DuckDB query · file I/O · blocking\nsql.py:179-206
    sub --> exec : rows; preview capped at SQL_PREVIEW_ROW_CAP (config.py:234)
    note over exec, store #FEE2E2
      **F3** — the synthesizer is handed `f"SQL result ({len(rows)} row(s)):"`
      followed by only `rows[:30]`, with **no statement that this is a sample**
      (agent.py:258-274). The direct SQL route carries an explicit "you are
      shown only the FIRST FEW ROWS, quote the true row count" instruction
      (sql.py:267-278), added because "314 rows came back and the summary said
      29 records". The agent path never got that fix.
    end note

  else kind == "rag" and salesforce
    exec -> store : select_context(step.input) → LanceDB vector search\nrag.py:91
    exec -> vmain : answer completion · temperature 0.2 · max_tokens 5000, then build_citations\nagent.py:281-285

  else kind == "salesforce" and salesforce  [the Salesforce gate]
    exec -> sf : fetch_live(step.input, history) — SOQL against the **live production org**\nHTTPS · JWT Bearer · SF_LIVE_TIMEOUT · agent.py:293, live_sf.py:140-145
    sf --> exec : rows → merge_rows + describe_rows (30-row cap, live_sf.py:148)
    note over exec, sf #FEE2E2
      Closed gate: when mode == "assistant" the planner is given
      _PLAN_SYSTEM_NO_SF and _coerce_no_salesforce rewrites every non-llm kind
      to "llm" (agent.py:131-160) — the gate is a **prompt plus a coercion**,
      not a runtime capability check.
      Degradation is invisible: SalesforceUnavailable / UnsafeSoql return a
      prose apology and an empty sub-meta, yet the step still reports
      status="done" (agent.py:294-303).
      **F6** — agent.py:312-335 is a byte-equivalent duplicate of this branch
      behind the identical condition: 24 lines of unreachable dead code.
    end note

  else kind == "web"
    exec -> web : research_step(step.input, history, effort, emit)\nsearch backend query + arbitrary page fetches chosen by the model\nagent.py:341-343
    exec -> fe : SSE · event: research\ndata: {"phase": "reading" | "read", "count": int}\nsearch.py:446, :454
    note over exec, web #FEE2E2
      **F4** — with **no sources** the branch has no `return` and **falls
      through** (agent.py:351-352) into the llm tail: the step answers from
      model knowledge, is reported status="done", and carries **no**
      search_unavailable flag — unlike the direct search route, which sets
      meta.search_unavailable = True (search.py:416).
      Fetched page content is untrusted and reaches the model prompt.
    end note

  else kind == "llm", or the web branch fell through
    exec -> vmain : chat_completion([_STEP_LLM_SYSTEM, recent_turns(history, 8), step.input])\ntemperature 0.3 · max_tokens 5000 · agent.py:357-364
  end

  alt the step raised
    exec -> fe : SSE · event: step\ndata: {"id", "title", "status": "failed", "detail": _shorten(str(exc), 200)}\nagent.py:387-392
    exec -> exec : output becomes "Step failed: <detail>"; the plan still "succeeds" as a whole;\nsibling steps are unaffected · agent.py:393-398
    note over exec, fe #FEE2E2
      **F5 — raw exception text is streamed to the browser** as step.detail
      (agent.py:388-392): stack-free but unsanitised, and it may carry SOQL,
      SQL, hostnames or driver messages. Nothing is logged server-side.
      This is one of eleven bare `except` sites in the core-4 engines, **none**
      of which log (evidence: orch-engines-core4.md).
    end note
  else the step succeeded
    exec -> fe : SSE · event: step\ndata: {"id", "title", "status": "done", "detail": <short summary>}\nagent.py:399-402
  end
end

exec -> exec : asyncio.gather(*(run(step) for step in plan.steps)) — **without return_exceptions=True**\nagent.py:405
note over exec #FEE2E2
  **F10** — because return_exceptions is not set, a BaseException that escapes
  run() (notably asyncio.CancelledError from POST /chat/stop, main.py:721)
  aborts the gather and leaves the sibling coroutines **still running** —
  their Salesforce queries and page fetches complete with nobody listening.
  Concurrent steps also share one `emit` callable, so research events from
  parallel web steps interleave into a single frontend panel with no step id
  (sse.ts:166-199).
end note
exec --> ag : List of {step, status, output, meta} — gather preserves plan order

== 3 · SYNTHESIZE — one merged answer, one merged meta ==

ag -> ag : renumber_web_sources(results) — mutates outputs and sub-metas in place,\n**before** the prompt is built, so plan-wide markers are what the model reads\nagent.py:411-452, :588
note over ag #FFFBEB
  Sources without a `url` are skipped (agent.py:435-437), leaving their local
  [n] markers unmapped and pointing at whichever page ends up with that
  plan-wide number.
end note

ag -> vmain : llm.stream_chat_events(_synthesis_messages(message, results),\nmodel_choice "smart" · temperature 0.2 · max_tokens _SYNTH_TOKENS: 6000 medium / 12000 high\nagent.py:591-597

loop for every streamed delta
  vmain --> ag : ("reasoning" | "token", delta)
  ag -> fe : SSE · event: reasoning\ndata: {"text": str}   ·   event: token\ndata: {"text": str}\nagent.py:599, :602
end

ag -> fe : SSE · the SINGLE final event: meta = merge_step_meta(results)\nroute "agent", steps[], plus sql/data/truncated/chart/chart_data, citations, sources, report_files\nagent.py:467-518, :605
note over ag, fe #FFFBEB
  merge_step_meta rules: the **last** step with a truthy `sql` contributes the
  whole _SQL_PAYLOAD_KEYS tuple atomically (agent.py:489-493); citations dedupe
  on record_id, report files on filename, sources on url (agent.py:494-510).
  Nothing enforces "exactly one meta per turn" at runtime — there is no engine
  ABC, no Protocol and no return-type check anywhere; the contract is pure duck
  typing re-declared per module (engines/__init__.py, chat.py:22, agent.py:34).
end note
ag --> orch : "".join(parts) → the answer string\nagent.py:606, :658

note over ag, web #FEE2E2
  **No timeout exists anywhere in agent.py.** `rg wait_for|timeout` over
  engines/*.py hits only url.py:36 and search.py:315/338. The single bound is
  the 300 s httpx client timeout (llm.py:78, config.py:264).
  Worst case for ONE user message: plan 2 x 300 s, then ceil(8/3) = 3 waves of
  (per-step model call + Salesforce/web fetch), then the synthesis stream —
  **well past 20 minutes**, with the only cancellation path being the user
  pressing Stop (POST /chat/stop → task.cancel(), main.py:716-722).
  Model-call budget at 8 steps: 1-2 plan + 1 per llm/rag/web step + 1-2 per sql
  step + 1 streaming synthesis = roughly **11-19 model calls per message**.
end note

